speechtext:
Bill (No. 207) to prohibit the importation, manufacture or sale of adulterated, process, or renovated butter, oleomargarine, butterine or other substitutes for butter and to prevent the improper marking of butter, read the second time, and House went into committee thereon.
On section 3,
In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires,-
(a)	' Creamery ' means a place where the milk or cream of not less than fifty cows is manufactured into butter ;
(b)	' Dairy ' means a place where the milk or cream of less than fifty cows is manufactured into butter ;
(c)	' Butter ' means the food product commonly known as butter, which is manufactured exclusively from milk or cream or both, with or without the addition of colouring matter, common salt or other harmless preservative ;
(d)	' Creamery butter ' means butter which is manufactured in a creamery ;
(e)	* Dairy butter ' means butter which is manufactured in a dairy.
(f)	Renovated butter ' or ' process butter * means any butter which has been melted, clarified or refined, and made to resemble butter.
